File: force-app/main/default/classes/ContactImportService.cls
```apex
public class ContactImportService {

    /**
     * Bulk-inserts legacy contacts in a single DML statement while bypassing
     * only TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask (after insert).  All other registered
     * Contact actions – in particular TA_Contact_FormatPhone (before insert) –
     * continue to run.
     *
     * The bypass is guaranteed to be removed before the method returns (via
     * the finally block), so any Contact inserted later in the same
     * transaction will receive its welcome task as usual.
     */
    public static void importContacts(List<Contact> contacts) {
        if (contacts == null || contacts.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Register a targeted bypass for the welcome-task action only.
        // TA_Bypass.skip() in TAF 0.3.4 adds the key 'Contact.TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask'
        // to the framework's internal bypass set; the trigger handler checks this
        // set before invoking each action.
        TA_Bypass.skip('Contact', 'TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask');

        try {
            // Single bulk DML statement – satisfies the "one DML" requirement
            // and lets TAF's before-insert action (TA_Contact_FormatPhone)
            // process every record in the list.
            insert contacts;
        } finally {
            // Clear the bypass so it does not leak into subsequent DML
            // operations in this transaction.  After this point, every
            // registered Contact action (including TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask)
            // will execute normally.
            TA_Bypass.clear();
        }
    }
}
```

**How it works, step-by-step:**

1. **`TA_Bypass.skip('Contact', 'TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask')`** – Adds the action key to TAF's internal static `Set<String>` bypass list. When the Contact `after insert` trigger fires and TAF iterates over registered actions, it calls `TA_Bypass.isBypassed('Contact', actionName)` for each. Because only the welcome-task key is present, `TA_Contact_FormatPhone` (before insert) and any other registered actions proceed normally; the welcome task is simply skipped.

2. **`insert contacts;`** – One bulk DML statement. The before-insert trigger fires first (formatting phones), then the insert, then the after-insert trigger fires but TAF short-circuits the welcome-task action due to the bypass.

3. **`TA_Bypass.clear()` in `finally`** – Removes all entries from the bypass set (including ours). Because the `finally` block runs before the method returns—even if the insert throws—the bypass is guaranteed to be gone. Any subsequent `insert` of Contact in the same transaction will execute the full set of registered actions, including `TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask`.

